Upgraded ``requests`` to 2.34.2 and ``urllib3`` to 2.x (sandialabs/PEAT#28). urllib3 2.x requires TLS 1.2, uses the system cipher list, and errors on responses shorter than their ``Content-Length``, which broke HTTP(S) with many older devices. All PEAT HTTP sessions now use :class:`~peat.protocols.http.LegacyHTTPAdapter`, which allows TLS 1.0/1.1 and legacy ciphers and accepts truncated responses with a warning. SSL certificate retrieval (``HTTP.get_ssl_certificate()``) now also works with TLS 1.0/1.1 devices. ``opensearch-py`` was updated to 2.8.0, since it no longer needs to stay on 2.6.
